            <abstract>
                <p>This miracle is the thirteenth miracle in Bausi’s edition. According to this miracle, sick women who had come to the 
                    miraculous spring to bath are set upon by two snakes. It turned out that one of them had failed to purify herself after menstruation.
                    Once she confessed her fault, the snakes vanished.</p>
            </abstract>
